        "expression": null,
        "license": "BSD-3-Clause",
        "classifiers": ["License :: OSI Approved :: GNU Lesser General Public License v3 (LGPLv3)"]
      },
      "note": "The bindings are BSD-3-Clause (`license`), but the wheel is not only the bindings. Its own dist-info/licenses/LICENSES_bundled.txt states: \"License for pi-heif binary wheels: LGPLv3, due to base library licenses\" — libheif and libde265, both LGPLv3, shipped as DLLs/shared objects alongside the Python code. That is what the LGPLv3 classifier is about, and why the compound expression is the honest record. Recorded as -only rather than -or-later because upstream writes \"LGPLv3\" without stating \"or later\", and the stricter reading is the safe one. This is also why PM pins pi-heif and not pillow-heif: same author, same repository, same API, but pillow-heif's wheels add the x265 HEVC encoder and are GPLv2 as a whole."
    },
